From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:28:30 -0700
Subject: nvme: apple: the T6050 ANS2 sleep attachment where the sleep is
 described

The attachment was made on two boards by name. Make it wherever the
device tree describes T6050's deep sleep; the node's own properties
still decide the rest.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple-m5-sleep.h | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple-m5-sleep.h b/drivers/nvme/host/apple-m5-sleep.h
index f22d6902bf2..50bcaeabde6 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple-m5-sleep.h
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple-m5-sleep.h
@@ -167,10 +167,8 @@ static int apple_nvme_m5_attach(struct apple_nvme *anv)
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	/* Both boards use T6050 ANS2's split NVMe/NVMMU layout and retained SART. */
-	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6050") ||
-	    (!of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s") &&
-	     !of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c")))
+	/* T6050 ANS2's split NVMe/NVMMU layout and retained SART, where the sleep is described. */
+	if (!apple_t6050_sleep_described())
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	/* The wait before the restart after a sleep comes from the DT; without it, no sleep. */
 	if (of_property_read_u32(anv->dev->of_node, "apple,sleep-wake-delay-ms",
